{
  "_createdAt": "2026-04-27T21:46:58Z",
  "_id": "wp-post-1470-en",
  "_rev": "Kra5TYIFOKLIQlRCd7qUKT",
  "_type": "article",
  "_updatedAt": "2026-07-05T14:24:52Z",
  "author": {
    "_ref": "author-legacy-archive",
    "_type": "reference"
  },
  "body": [
    {
      "_key": "000000000001",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000000",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Egypt is a country used to travellers."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000003",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "4y14zkr6b9bz",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "z4jozjk9290a"
          ],
          "text": "Cairo"
        },
        {
          "_key": "edltb8evjdu0",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": ", "
        },
        {
          "_key": "nikpzp8mjbuk",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "mmwyivpqbsfg"
          ],
          "text": "Giza"
        },
        {
          "_key": "dgylraa7oi1m",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": ", "
        },
        {
          "_key": "zuwxniujvlcf",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "6cquwp4kzzkk"
          ],
          "text": "Luxor"
        },
        {
          "_key": "cgmfgdwvnbw3",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": ", "
        },
        {
          "_key": "qj7owo0pa66q",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "nvrczngixr09"
          ],
          "text": "Aswan"
        },
        {
          "_key": "8pnihlqsumt1",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": ", the Red Sea. Foreign visitors are familiar everywhere. So a small Arabic slip, a hesitant handshake, or imperfect dress does not break the trip."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [
        {
          "_key": "z4jozjk9290a",
          "_type": "internalLink",
          "reference": {
            "_ref": "wp-page-83284",
            "_type": "reference"
          }
        },
        {
          "_key": "mmwyivpqbsfg",
          "_type": "internalLink",
          "reference": {
            "_ref": "wp-page-58854",
            "_type": "reference"
          }
        },
        {
          "_key": "6cquwp4kzzkk",
          "_type": "internalLink",
          "reference": {
            "_ref": "wp-page-58877",
            "_type": "reference"
          }
        },
        {
          "_key": "nvrczngixr09",
          "_type": "internalLink",
          "reference": {
            "_ref": "wp-page-58758",
            "_type": "reference"
          }
        }
      ],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000005",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000004",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Don't lean too hard on that tolerance."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000007",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000006",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Egypt carries social senses around hospitality, family, religion, respect for elders, and pride in the country. What's asked of travellers is not to become someone else. It is to read the air of the place."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000009",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000008",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "What matters is not memorising \"don'ts.\" It is knowing why something matters."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000000b",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000000a",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Use a little Arabic"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h2"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000000d",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000000c",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "A little Arabic goes a long way in Egypt."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000000f",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000000e",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "You don't need to be perfect. The traveller's clumsy attempt itself reads as friendly."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000011",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000010",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "A few words to remember."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000013",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000012",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "\"Shukran\" — thank you."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000015",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000014",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "\"La, shukran\" — no, thank you. The most useful for declining touts and sales."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000017",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000016",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "\"Ahlan\" — a warm hello, welcome."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000019",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000018",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "\"Ma'a salama\" — goodbye, take care, on parting."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000001b",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000001a",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "\"Inshallah\" — if God wills. Not only a way to soften promises; an everyday expression that includes the sense that things are not decided by humans alone."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000001d",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000001c",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "\"Alhamdulillah\" — thanks to God; used in \"I'm well,\" \"good,\" \"thankfully.\""
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000001f",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000001e",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "A few words soften the start of a conversation. Egyptians are very tolerant of foreign pronunciation. What matters is not skill but the posture of meeting the other's language."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000021",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000020",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Dress by place"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h2"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000023",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000022",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Egyptian dress varies considerably by place."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000025",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000024",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "On Red Sea resort beaches, swimwear and resort wear are normal. At the hotel pool, private beach, and on boat trips, the international resort feel is fine."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000027",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000026",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Outside the hotel — in town, at sites, in markets, at religious sites — be a little more modest. Covering shoulders and knees is safe for both men and women. In Cairo, Luxor, Aswan, the countryside, and at mosques or churches, it looks natural."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000029",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000028",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Not only a women's issue. Men walking shirtless in town or entering religious sites in short shorts should be avoided."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000002b",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000002a",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Dress is not a morality test. It is a tool to reduce friction. In a hot country, thin long sleeves, linen, and loose clothing help."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000002d",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000002c",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Be quiet at religious sites"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h2"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000002f",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000002e",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Egypt has mosques, Coptic churches, monasteries, synagogues, and saints' shrines."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000031",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000030",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Cover shoulders and knees; in mosques, take off shoes. In churches too, quiet conduct is needed by place. Avoid moving forward during prayer, photographing people in prayer, speaking loudly, using flash."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000033",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000032",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Mosques and churches are places of faith before they are tourism. Being able to enter as a visitor is already on trust."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000035",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000034",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "In Ramadan, some consideration is needed. Travellers don't need to fast. You can eat at hotels and tourist restaurants. Avoid conspicuously eating, drinking, or smoking in public during the day."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000037",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000036",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Ramadan Egypt is a little quieter by day and lively after sunset. Less a difficult period; understood properly, very memorable."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000039",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000038",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Confirm before photographing"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h2"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000003b",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000003a",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Egypt makes you want to take pictures."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000003d",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000003c",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "You can't photograph everything."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000003f",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000003e",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Don't photograph military facilities, police, checkpoints, airport security areas, government buildings. This is not etiquette — it is law and safety."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000041",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000040",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "For people, ask. Especially with women, children, the religious, those praying, and people in poor neighbourhoods — don't shoot them as \"good pictures\" without permission. At tourist sites, some who pose expect a tip. That isn't unusual. Confirming first avoids dispute later."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000043",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "2k6c5z2o6ms1",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "At sites and museums, rules differ by place. No flash, no tripod, separate ticket required, no photography at all. Confirm at the "
        },
        {
          "_key": "e9a0h2ccsbaa",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "92eje2kq5ymn"
          ],
          "text": "Valley of the Kings"
        },
        {
          "_key": "hxrvbgk7qdqp",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": " and museums especially."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [
        {
          "_key": "92eje2kq5ymn",
          "_type": "internalLink",
          "reference": {
            "_ref": "guideArticle.luxor.valley-of-the-kings",
            "_type": "reference"
          }
        }
      ],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000045",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000044",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "When in doubt, don't shoot. Safest."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000047",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000046",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Touts and bargaining"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h2"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000049",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000048",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "There are sales pitches at Egyptian tourist sites."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000004b",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "df4p4idyvw4c",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Giza, "
        },
        {
          "_key": "jxh2wsw0cf8k",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "55a2afe0t1ua"
          ],
          "text": "Khan el-Khalili"
        },
        {
          "_key": "f2qxwjestbr7",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": ", parts of Luxor, around cruise boats. Souvenirs, camels, carriages, guides, taxis, photos. Strong calls."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [
        {
          "_key": "55a2afe0t1ua",
          "_type": "internalLink",
          "reference": {
            "_ref": "guideArticle.cairo.khan-el-khalili",
            "_type": "reference"
          }
        }
      ],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000004d",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000004c",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "The phrase you'll use most is \"la, shukran.\" No, thank you. Smile, say it once, keep walking. The easiest."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000004f",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000004e",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Long conversation without intent to buy reads to the other side as negotiation. Reacting in anger ruins the mood. Decline short, clear, without hostility."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000051",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000050",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Where there's bargaining, confirm first. For a camel or carriage, set price, time, route, and tipping. For a taxi, set the price or use the meter before departure. For souvenirs, only bargain on things you intend to buy."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000053",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000052",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Don't think of bargaining as only winning. Finishing at a price both sides feel good about is the best."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000055",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000054",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Don't dismiss hospitality"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h2"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000057",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000056",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Hospitality matters in Egypt."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000059",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000058",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Tea is offered. Food is offered. You're told to sit. Someone gives directions. These are not only services — they are social warmth."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000005b",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000005a",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "You don't have to accept everything. With no time, decline. Better than declining bluntly is declining with thanks."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000005d",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000005c",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "\"Shukran, but I'm fine.\""
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000005f",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000005e",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "That is enough."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000061",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000060",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "If invited to someone's home, watch whether shoes come off. If served food, eat at least a little. Bringing sweets or fruit is a good choice. Flowers can carry mourning or hospital associations depending on context — not always safe."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000063",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000062",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Handshake and distance"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h2"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000065",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000064",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Greeting matters in Egypt."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000067",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000066",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Between men, a handshake is normal. Among close acquaintances, cheek greetings happen. A foreign traveller can follow the other's lead."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000069",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000068",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "A handshake between men and women depends on the person. Conservative people may avoid handshakes with the opposite gender. Not rejection — religious and social sensibility."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000006b",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000006a",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "When a male traveller meets an Egyptian woman, waiting for her to extend a hand is natural. For female travellers, the other may hesitate. A smile and greeting are not rude even without a handshake."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000006d",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000006c",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Public expression of affection should be modest. Holding hands is common at tourist sites; hugging or kissing — pick your place. Red Sea resorts and provincial towns carry completely different air."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000006f",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000006e",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Conversation cautions"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h2"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000071",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000070",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Many Egyptians enjoy conversation."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000073",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000072",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Country of origin, family, work, football, food, Egyptian history. Easy entries. Praising Egyptian food, asking about places visited, asking for recommendations make conversation natural."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000075",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000074",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Politics — careful. Modern Egyptian politics is complex; views split even inside families and friend groups. If Egyptians start it, listen. Travellers don't need to import conclusions."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000077",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000076",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Religion is the same. You can ask with interest. Don't try to argue. Talking about Islam, the Coptic Church, faith, fasting, and prayer wants a listening posture."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000079",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000078",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Football is a strong topic. Al Ahly–Zamalek rivalry, the Egyptian national team, Mohamed Salah. Without interest, don't speak dismissively. If unsure, \"which team do you support?\" is enough."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000007b",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000007a",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Tipping and gratitude"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h2"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000007d",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000007c",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "In Egypt, tipping is part of the trip."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000007f",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000007e",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Hotel porter, driver, guide, restroom attendant, boat staff, restaurant. Amounts vary; small notes ready helps."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000081",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000080",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Tipping is not a large transaction with everyone. Where you receive service, giving nothing reads strangely. Confirm typical amounts with a guide or hotel in advance."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000083",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000082",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Don't see tipping only as \"annoying demand.\" It's part of Egypt's service economy. You also don't need to respond to every aggressive request. Separate moments of gratitude from moments of declining."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000085",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000084",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "A practical note for women travellers"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h2"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000087",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000086",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Women travellers can enjoy Egypt."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000089",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000088",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Stares and calls can be tiring in crowded places, markets, around tourist sites, and walking alone at night."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000008b",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000008a",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Dress modestly. Use trusted cars or ride-hailing and hotel arrangements. Don't walk lightly populated places late at night. Don't over-respond to persistent calls; decline clearly. Move toward a shop, a hotel, or near security if needed."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000008d",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000008c",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "The Cairo Metro has women-only cars — useful when crowded."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000008f",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000008e",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "You don't need to be afraid. In Egyptian urban space, moving with confidence matters. Better than stopping uncertain, decide a destination and walk. If needed, use a guide or driver."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000091",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000090",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Better described as \"best avoided\""
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h2"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000093",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000092",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Avoid these in Egypt:"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000095",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000094",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Speaking loudly inside religious sites."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000097",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000096",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Photographing people in prayer without permission."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000099",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000098",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Photographing police or checkpoints."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000009b",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000009a",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Long bargaining with no intent to buy."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000009d",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000009c",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Conspicuous eating or drinking in public during Ramadan daytime."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000009f",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000009e",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Imposing political conclusions from outside."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "0000000000a1",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "0000000000a0",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Joking about people's faith or dress."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "0000000000a3",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "0000000000a2",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Photographing children or women without permission."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "0000000000a5",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "0000000000a4",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Walking into town in resort clothing."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "0000000000a7",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "0000000000a6",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "None are particularly difficult. Ordinary respect."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "0000000000a9",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "0000000000a8",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "A frame that eases the trip"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h2"
    },
    {
      "_key": "0000000000ab",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "0000000000aa",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "In Egypt, posture is seen more than perfect etiquette."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "0000000000ad",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "0000000000ac",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Use a little Arabic. Say thanks. Be quiet in religious places. Don't photograph people without asking. Decline short and without hostility. Don't easily judge a country's politics or faith."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "0000000000af",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "0000000000ae",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "That alone changes the trip considerably."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "0000000000b1",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "0000000000b0",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Egypt is used to travellers' small mistakes. To travellers who move with respect, it responds even better."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "0000000000b3",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "0000000000b2",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Etiquette is not for tension."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "0000000000b5",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "0000000000b4",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "It is the tool for stepping into the place."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    }
  ],
